Package: PsyML
Type: Package
Title: Machine Learning Workflows for Supervised, Unsupervised, and Causal Analysis
Version: 2.4.2
Date: 2026-10-25
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jose", "Ventura-Leon",
           email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
    )
Description: Provides single-function pipelines for applied machine learning
    with tabular data, as commonly found in psychological, behavioral, and
    health research. The supervised pipeline, supervised_ml(), performs
    exploratory checks, preprocessing, training of several models with
    cross-validation, hyperparameter tuning, test-set evaluation, threshold
    optimization, calibration, fairness analysis, decision curve analysis,
    and model interpretation with permutation importance and Shapley values.
    The unsupervised pipeline, unsupervised_ml(), covers k-means,
    hierarchical, DBSCAN, Gaussian mixture, and latent class clustering with
    selection of the number of clusters, dimensionality reduction (PCA,
    t-SNE, UMAP), and anomaly detection (isolation forest, local outlier
    factor, Mahalanobis distance). The causal pipeline, causal_ml(), estimates
    treatment effects with propensity scores, meta-learners, double machine
    learning, causal forests, and targeted maximum likelihood estimation.
    Also includes learning-curve based sample size estimation, block and
    diversity-based data splitting, and export of results to text and JSON.
